# Security headers, served by Cloudflare for every path.
#
# Finding [MEDIUM] "No Content-Security-Policy or security headers on the web
# app" from the security audit.
#
# The Supabase session — access token and refresh token — lives in
# localStorage, which any script running on this origin can read. That is the
# standard trade-off for a browser app and is documented in
# app/lib/sessionStorage.ts, but it means a single injected script is durable
# account access to someone's health data and progress photos. A CSP is what
# stops a script that is not ours from running at all.
#
# script-src is 'self' with no 'unsafe-inline': the export emits exactly one
# external <script> and no inline ones, so nothing legitimate needs the escape
# hatch. style-src does need 'unsafe-inline' — the shell carries two inline
# <style> blocks and React Native Web injects rules at runtime. Inline styles
# are a far weaker vector than inline scripts.
#
# connect-src is the API and Supabase, the only two hosts this app talks to.
# img-src includes the Supabase host because progress photos are fetched from
# signed storage URLs, and blob:/data: because the picker previews locally
# before upload.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob: https://fdidttqeqwgozfuwdwjh.supabase.co; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https://fdidttqeqwgozfuwdwjh.supabase.co https://clever-contentment-production-bcb7.up.railway.app; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; object-src 'none'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
